  "notes": "The noun {着火|ちゃっか} (ignition) + する. Can be intransitive ('something catches fire') or transitive ('to set something alight'); the thing lit is marked with に.\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS:\n- ~に{着火|ちゃっか}する: to ignite ~\n- ~が{着火|ちゃっか}する: ~ catches fire\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {点火|てんか}する: to ignite; to light — a near-synonym, common for engines and burners\n- {火|ひ}をつける: to set fire to — the plain, everyday phrasing",
